{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the people saw and they trembled</b> — therefore one sways during Torah study, for the Torah was given in awe, in trembling, and in sweating." "<b>וינועו</b> in gematria = 12 milin (miles), that they recoiled backward." "<b>וינועו</b> — twice in the Masorah: here and \"וינועו אמות הספים מקול הקורא\" — just as there it was by an angel, so too here by angels, as written: \"מלכי צבאות ידודון ידודון\" (kings of hosts will flee, will flee)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {2 "The second Masorah occurrence is from 1 Samuel 5:5; the verse from Psalms 68:13."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:45.492465404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}